[] #2: Loadstones

[hairston@henry.ece.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:]
[] when dropped always becomes re-cursed, that's its magic ...
[] cursed - can be picked up and becomes extra heavy, can't be dropped/thrown.
[] uncursed - normal weight, can be dropped/thrown as a stone.
[] blessed - has negative weight, forces levitation if you're not carrying
[]    enough (you'd have to drop the stone to get down, oh no it's
[]    cursed again ...).
...
[] here's an oppurtunity to knock a stupid of mine:
...
[] ring of levitation: reverses your levitation stat.

i keep getting this vision of a poor hapless hacker blessing his (or her)
loadstone only to find that using the potion has reduced his carrying
weight under the levitation limit and so begins to float.  being clever
he uses his ring of levitation to float down and picks up a scroll of
identify which immediately causes him to float back up again since the
weight limit for the blessed loadstone has been breached and he's wearing
a ring of levitation.  he reads the scroll, floats back down ... and so on.

btw, i have to think some more about loadstones always being cursed when
dropped.  in any event, a blessed loadstone should counter the weight
penalty of a cursed loadstone (except by the weight of two stones and
should still impose a minimum carrying weight limit.)

